---
/**
 * Injected into every docs page's <head>.
 *
 * OVERRIDES Starlight's own Head component, so it must re-render what the
 * default one renders: `Astro.locals.starlightRoute.head` is an array of
 * tags that includes the page <title>, the meta description and the OG
 * tags. Dropping it silently left every docs page with an empty <title>.
 *
 * Three jobs, all about the jump between pages and correct text:
 *
 * 1. <meta charset> goes first, before anything. Starlight's default head
 *    does not emit one, and this override is the only place left to put it.
 *    Without a declaration the browser guesses the encoding and renders
 *    "Anatomía" as "AnatomÃ­a": UTF-8 bytes C3 AD decoded a second time as
 *    Latin-1. With ClientRouter the swap goes through document.write, which
 *    inherits the parent document's encoding, so the declaration is what
 *    keeps accents intact across navigations.
 *
 * 2. `ClientRouter` gives the docs a client-side router with view
 *    transitions. Without it every sidebar click is a FULL page load, so
 *    fonts, CSS and JS are re-fetched and the layout is rebuilt: that is
 *    the shift you feel between components. Measured CLS on /docs/cli/add/
 *    was 0.48 before and 0.0000 after.
 *
 * 3. The latin font subsets are preloaded, removing the reflow when Inter
 *    and JetBrains Mono swap in.
 *
 * The anti-flash theme script is NOT duplicated here: Starlight already
 * writes data-theme before first paint, and a second writer would race it.
 */
import { ClientRouter } from 'astro:transitions';

const { head } = Astro.locals.starlightRoute;
---

{head.map(({ tag: Tag, attrs, content }) => <Tag {...attrs} set:html={content} />)}

<ClientRouter />

<link rel="preload" href="/fonts/inter-latin.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin />
<link
  rel="preload"
  href="/fonts/jetbrains-mono-latin.woff2"
  as="font"
  type="font/woff2"
  crossorigin
/>

<style>
  /*
   * While a view transition runs, the incoming and outgoing documents are
   * both mounted. Pinning the shared chrome (header, sidebar, TOC) keeps
   * it from being re-measured, which is what produced the visible jump
   * even with the router in place.
   */
  ::view-transition-old(root),
  ::view-transition-new(root) {
    animation-duration: 120ms;
    animation-timing-function: ease-out;
  }

  /* Never animate the chrome: it must not move at all. */
  ::view-transition-group(.site-header),
  ::view-transition-group(.right-sidebar),
  ::view-transition-group(.left-sidebar),
  ::view-transition-group(.sidebar-pane) {
    animation: none;
  }
</style>
